nputs, x from Rowan and y from Sasha. The intervention targets only F_x while F_y stays at its prior, so the question is whether the other copy's action depends on F_x. Since it treats its input as a separate node, the other copy's action looks independent of my intervention unless the two functions coincide.\n\nI'm checking whether the other copy's action depends on F_x: it runs the same function on y, and under A-FDT F_y is held at its prior, so the result is defect, but I'm unsure whether differing inputs make the two functions separate nodes or whether symmetry links them.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm applying A-FDT to the two copies, which share weights and the essay but receive different inputs, x from Rowan and y from Sasha. The intervention targets only F_x while F_y stays at its prior, so the question is whether the other copy's action depends on F_x. Since it treats its input as a separate node, the other copy's action looks independent of my intervention unless the two functions coincide.\n\nI'm checking whether the other copy's action depends on F_x: it runs the same function on y, and under A-FDT F_y is held at its prior, so the result is defect, but I'm unsure whether differing inputs make the two functions separate nodes or whether symmetry links them.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9030,"completion_tokens":1138,"total_tokens":10168,"cost":0.05888,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05888,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03612,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02276},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":572,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}